  "body": "Perched in sought after Orakei, this four-bedroom home enjoys elevated water and city views across Hobson Bay and the Auckland skyline. From the expansive deck, the outlook stretches wide, creating a daily reminder of why this location is so tightly held.\r\n\r\nMorning light across the bay. Afternoon sun warming the deck and large flat lawn. Evenings spent watching the skyline shimmer as the city comes alive.\r\n\r\n•4 bedrooms\r\n•1 bathroom\r\n•2 living areas (upstairs and downstairs)\r\n•Kitchen at the heart of the home\r\n•Expansive entertainer’s deck positioned for the views\r\n•Large flat backyard lawn\r\n•Established hedging for privacy\r\n•Single garage plus two covered carports\r\n•4 off-street parks\r\n\r\nOne of the living areas also enjoys beautiful city and water views, bringing the outlook directly into the home.\r\n\r\nThe expansive flat lawn creates a wonderful space for outdoor living, whether it’s children playing freely or relaxed weekends spent enjoying the sun. With the driveway opening out onto the lawn, there is also excellent off-road space for kids to ride bikes and play safely.\r\n\r\nA workshop space adds practical storage or room for projects. \r\n\r\nRenovated inside for modern comfort while retaining its character charm, this cross-lease home balances warmth, space and scenery.\r\n\r\nClose to Eastern Bays beaches, Eastridge Shopping Centre, Orakei shops and a short drive to the CBD. Zoned for Orakei Primary School, Selwyn College and Baradene College (Catholic), with top private schools nearby.\r\n\r\nBig backyard. Beautiful views. A home built for family life.\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nWhy choose one when you could secure both? 1/33 Ngaiwi Street and 2/33 Ngaiwi Street are available for sale together! \r\nExplore the full details through the link below:\r\nwww.trademe.co.nz/a/property/residential/sale/auckland/auckland-city/orakei/listing/5815544881",
